{
  "_comment": [
    "THE TOOL ROSTER SERVED IN PRODUCTION (Task 11.10.2).",
    "",
    "This is the `allowed_tools` list on the Composio MCP server named by",
    "`mcp.server_id` in config.yaml. It is the ONLY record of what that server",
    "serves, and it matters because `allowed_tools` CANNOT be updated in place:",
    "the SDK's mcp.update answers ValidationError and every REST path is a 404.",
    "Changing the roster means MINTING A NEW SERVER from this file and pointing",
    "mcp.server_id at it, then deleting the old one (an account caps at ~16).",
    "",
    "Nothing reads this at runtime -- Composio enforces the list server-side.",
    "It is here so a roster change is reviewable in a diff rather than",
    "reconstructed from a live server, and so the server can be rebuilt if it is",
    "ever lost.",
    "",
    "Curated from 1442 available: read-mostly cores, no permanent deletes",
    "(GMAIL_DELETE_MESSAGE, LINEAR_DELETE_LINEAR_ISSUE, GOOGLEDRIVE_EMPTY_TRASH,",
    "GOOGLECALENDAR_CLEAR_CALENDAR), no arbitrary query escape hatch",
    "(LINEAR_RUN_QUERY_OR_MUTATION), no settings/admin surface, and one framing",
    "per operation where the vendor offers several.",
    "",
    "205 tools against a connector budget of 105 (llm.max_tools 128 minus 23 of",
    "ours): all seven CANNOT be enabled at once, and 11.5 benches whole servers",
    "most-recently-enabled first. That is the owner's route-B ruling, 2026-08-26."
  ],
